      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1699818361/performances/MCC18IS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "TIFF Film Circuit: Once Upon a Time in a Cinema"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p>The Colchester Film Society is thrilled to continue our TIFF: Film Circuit screenings at The Marigold Cultural Centre with a movie made specifically for people who love the magic of the big screen: David Gleeson's heartfelt and hilarious dramedy, <b><i>Once Upon a Time in a Cinema!</i></b></p><br>\n\n<p>Set in a cozy Irish town in the 1980s, the film follows Earl Clancy (played by the fantastic Colin Morgan), a cinema manager trying to survive the Friday night shift from absolute hell. In real tim, over the course of a single, chaotic 90-minute screening—Earl has to put out literal and figurative fires while deciding whether to sell his beloved theatre to a shady local politician.</p><br>\n\n<p>If you've ever worked in customer service, or if you just love the nostalgic, crackling energy of an old-school movie house, this is the ultimate feel-good watch. It's a beautifully shot, funny, and deeply affectionate love letter to the local cinemas that hold our communities together.</p><br>\n\n<p>Grab your popcorn and join us for another cozy, unforgettable night of movie magic at the Marigold!</p>\n\n\n<style>\n@media screen and (max-width: 600px){iframe{width:100%;}}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
