      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "PEACEMAKER: Outlaw Country"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p>PEACEMAKER Good old-fashioned outlaw country.\nDusty trails, campfires, old guitars and fast horses. Wide open skies and dark smoky\nhonky-tonks. Good whiskey, bad heartaches and great music. This is outlaw country.The\nScott Macaulay Performing Arts Centre is beyond pleased to announce the debut show of\nPEI's own outlaw country band PEACEMAKER October 8, 2026</p> \n<p>Forged recently in the flames of their true love for old time, outlaw country music,\nPEACEMAKER is composed of six of PEI's most highly respected and sought after\nmusicians. Aron Scott on guitars and vocals, Katy Currie on acoustic guitar and vocals,\nDan Currie on guitars and vocals, Stephane Bouchard on bass, Johnny Ross on piano and\nRoger Carter on drums. Coming together from areas, spanning nearly the entirety of the\nprovince, they make their real home on the stage and are hereby inviting you over to hoot\nand holler with them.</p> \n<p>You can expect to hear a whole lot of your favourite from around 1980 back in time, all\nclassics in the truest sense of the word. PEACEMAKER is going to give you a bit of\neverything from Merle to Loretta, Willie to Hank, Jerry, and of course, ol' Waylon.\nCome on out and stay a while, raise a glass and raise a ruckus, October 8, 2026 at the\nScott Macaulay Performing Arts Centre with PEACEMAKER your friendly neighbourhood\noutlaw country band.</p> \n\n\n<style>\n.location-page-temp {\n    display: block!important;\n}\n</style>"
      }
