    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1696980947/performances/AST30JS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1696980947/performances/AST30JS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "\"Hello Again\" featuring the music of Neil Diamond - with Sean Andrews"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p> <b>A life story told through the music of Neil Diamond\n</b><br>\nBoardwalk Productions is excited to bring Sean Andrews in 'Hello Again' featuring the music of Neil Diamond, to the Astor Theatre for an unforgettable evening of story, song, and nostalgia. This powerful musical experience has played to sold-out audiences, earning standing ovations and glowing reviews wherever it appears.</p>\n\n<p>\nHello Again is far more than a tribute concert—it is a deeply personal musical journey through memory, love, and connection. As each iconic Neil Diamond song fills the room, it unlocks a chapter of Sean's life, reminding us how music becomes the soundtrack to our most meaningful moments. Through humour, resilience, nostalgia, and tenderness, the songs carry the audience through a powerful story of family and the enduring bond between a mother and her sons. It is a reminder that music doesn't just entertain—it preserves who we were, who we loved, and how we became who we are.'An outstanding show. We left humming and singing our favourite Neil Diamond songs, and we continued to do so all night.'</p>\n\n<p><b>\n'The band was just WOW.'</b></p>\n\n<p>\nSean Andrews hails from Cole Harbour, Nova Scotia. A graduate of the Music Theatre Performance Program at Sheridan College in Ontario, Sean has been a professional performer for over 25 years. Favourite roles include Harry Houdini in the world premiere of Houdini the Musical in the UK, Ensemble in the North American premiere of Mamma Mia! in Toronto, and Glenn Guglia in the Canadian premiere of The Wedding Singer at Stage West. Sean also spent a decade travelling the world as a lead vocalist aboard Carnival, Norwegian, and Celebrity Cruise Lines, captivating audiences across the globe.\n'I hope many, many more people get to enjoy this story.'</p>\n\n\n<p>Directed by Edmund McLean, the production is guided by a deep understanding of both performance and education. Edmund's directing credits include For Whom the Gods Would Destroy, Fiddler on the Roof, Broadway Bound, Rent, Man of La Mancha, and Roy Orbison's In Dreams.'We were totally blown away. Every minute was fun, haunting, interesting, and a pleasure to the ears.'\n</p>\n\n\n\n<style>\n\n@media screen and (max-width:728px) {\niframe{width:100%!important;}\n}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
